  "title": "rapid-hemifield-object-eeg",
  "description": "EEG recordings from participants viewing object and word stimuli presented in rapid serial streams at 5 Hz to the left visual field, the right visual field, or centrally. Participants performed an orthogonal red target detection task while stimuli were shown. The dataset supports investigation of the temporal dynamics of visual object coding within and across the cerebral hemispheres, particularly for objects in peripheral vision.",
  "methods_description": "Object and word stimuli were presented at a rapid rate of 5Hz in the left or right visual field or centrally, while participants performed an orthogonal red target detection task, with EEG recorded throughout.",
